//! Database rebuild and reindexing from files (TF-019).
//!
//! Regenerates all derived SQLite tables from files on disk in one atomic,
//! cancellable transaction while preserving all durable history tables.
//!
//! ## Derived tables regenerated by a rebuild
//! - `projects`
//! - `agents`
//! - `agent_paths`
//! - `items`
//! - `item_versions`
//! - `native_items`
//! - `deployments`
//! - `locks`
//! - `sources`
//! - `presets`
//! - `preset_members`
//! - `secret_refs`
//! - `secret_ref_uses`
//! - `remote_backup_state`
//!
//! ## History tables preserved across rebuilds
//! - `operations`
//! - `operation_files`
//! - `backups`
//! - `health_checks`
//! - `drift_events`
//! - `preset_applications`
//! - `preset_application_members`
//! - `settings`
//!
//! ## Rebuild lifecycle
//! 1. Snapshot row counts for history and derived tables.
//! 2. Mark rebuild running in `settings` (key `rebuild.state`).
//! 3. Open an immediate transaction (`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`).
//! 4. Delete derived rows inside the transaction.
//! 5. Scan stores and agent directories from disk (or use supplied input).
//! 6. Insert new derived rows.
//! 7. Verify invariants (e.g. linked deployments target existing items).
//! 8. Update `rebuild.state` to completed and commit the transaction.
//!
//! If any error occurs or the operation is cancelled, the transaction is rolled back,
//! leaving the previous derived data intact.

